# Source material: study and screening PDFs, theses, applications, screening
# images, methodological reference papers. This repository is public and most of
# this material is copyright, so none of it belongs in version control.
dissertation_shared_folder/
methods/
*.pdf
*.docx
*.xlsx
*.png
*.jpg
*.jpeg

# Derived figures are deliberately not versioned. The figure-generating code and
# the machine-readable tables behind each figure are the artefacts of record, so
# a reader reproduces a figure rather than trusting a committed image.

# Fitted models and compiled Stan artefacts. The .stan and .R sources are the
# artefacts; the binaries are machine-specific and large.
.cache/
*.rds
*.o
*.so
*.dylib

# R session detritus. The renv lockfile is committed; the library is not.
.Rhistory
.RData
.Rproj.user/
renv/library/
renv/local/
renv/python/
renv/sandbox/
renv/staging/

# Python bytecode. The .py sources under scripts/ are the artefacts; the caches
# are written whenever one script imports another and are machine-specific.
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Platform noise.
.DS_Store
*~
private/

# Internal working documents. Reviews, assistant instructions and execution
# plans are working notes, not part of the public record of the review. The
# record of what was decided belongs in docs/methods_deviations.md and the
# commit history; these files are the scaffolding that got us there, and they
# quote unredacted contact details and draft wording that has not been checked.
CLAUDE.md
BAYESIAN_META_ANALYSIS_PLAN_FEASIBILITY_REVIEW.md
DEFINITIVE_EXTRACTION_PLAN_REVIEW.md
POST_STAGE_F_PLAN_REVIEW_2026-08-13.md
EXECUTION_PLAN_2026-08-13.md

# Engineering fits run on synthetic data and are never results.
results/engineering_*/
